<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN NATIONS CUP COLLATED RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN NATIONS CUP COLLATED RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of the final round of African Nations Cup qualifying matches at the weekend:</p>
<p>Group one:</p>
<p>In Luanda:</p>
<p>Angola 2 Zimbabwe 1 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Abgola - Paulao (10th minute), Akwa (70th)</p>
<p>Zimbabwe - Stewart Murisa (78th)</p>
<p>Attendance:</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under matches played, won, drew, lost, goals for, goals against, points):</p>
<p>    Ghana     4  2  1  1  4  3  7</p>
<p>    Angola    4  2  0  2  4  4  6</p>
<p>    Zimbabwe  4  1  1  2  3  4  4</p>
<p>Ghana and Angola qualify</p>
<p>Group two:</p>
<p>In Algiers:</p>
<p>Algeria 2 Benin 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Abdelhafid Tasfaout (13th), Cheikh Benzerga (27th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20000</p>
<p>In Bouake:</p>
<p>Ivory Coast 4 Mali 2 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ivory Coast - Joel Tiehi (22nd, 26th), Guel Tchiressoa (51st), Ibrahim Bakayoko (75th)</p>
<p>Mali - Soumalia Coulibaly (47th min), Modibo Sidibe (69th min penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance: 10000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast   6  4  1  1  10 8  13</p>
<p>    Algeria	 6  3  1  2  9  5  10</p>
<p>    Mali	    6  3  0  3  9  9  9</p>
<p>    Benin	   6  0  2  4  3  9  2</p>
<p>Ivory Coast and Algeria qualify</p>
<p>Group three:</p>
<p>In Cairo:</p>
<p>Egypt 8 Ethiopia 1 (5-0)</p>
<p>Attendance: 60000</p>
<p>In Rabat:</p>
<p>Morocco 3 Senegal 0 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Salaheddine Bassir (11th min, 67th min), Saidi Chiba (40th min)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20000</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Morocco    6  4  2  0  10 2  14</p>
<p>    Egypt	6  2  3  1  12 4  9</p>
<p>    Senegal    6  2  2  2  5  6  8</p>
<p>    Ethiopia   6  0  1  5  3  20 1</p>
<p>Morocco and Egypt qualify</p>
<p>Group four:</p>
<p>Final standings:</p>
<p>    Tunisia	 3  2  0  1  3  1  6</p>
<p>    Guinea	  3  2  0  1  2  1  6</p>
<p>    Sierra Leone  2  0  0  2  0  3  0</p>
<p>Sierra Leone withdrew from last two matches; Tunisia and Guinea qualify</p>
<p>Group five:</p>
<p>In Yaounde:</p>
<p>Cameroon 1 Kenya 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Cameroon - Fabrice Moreau (89th min penalty)</p>
<p>Kenya - Francis Were (49th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 30000</p>
<p>In Libreville:</p>
<p>Gabon 1 Namibia 1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Gabon - Pierre Aubame (22nd min penalty)</p>
<p>Namibia - Johannes Hindjou (60th min penalty)</p>
<p>Attendance:</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Cameroon    6  2  4  0  8  3  10</p>
<p>    Namibia     6  2  2  2  4  7  8</p>
<p>    Gabon	 6  1  4  1  5  5  7</p>
<p>    Kenya	 6  1  2  3  2  4  5</p>
<p>Cameroon and Namibia qualify</p>
<p>Group six:</p>
<p>In Kinshasa:</p>
<p>DR Congo (formerly Zaire) 1 Togo 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Nzangadi Kidoda (15th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 60000</p>
<p>In Monrovia:</p>
<p>Liberia 1 Tanzania 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Zizi Roberts (54th)</p>
<p>Attendance:</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>    Togo		    6  3  1  2  9  5  10</p>
<p>    DR Congo (ex Zaire) 6  2  3  1  6  5  9</p>
<p>    Liberia		 6  2  2  2  5  8  8</p>
<p>    Tanzania		6  1  2  3  5  7  5</p>
<p>Togo and DR Congo qualify</p>
<p>Group seven:</p>
<p>In Chililabombwe:</p>
<p>Zambia 1 Mauritius 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Vincent Mutale (57th minute)</p>
<p>Attendance: 20000</p>
<p>In Maputo:</p>
<p>Mozambique 2 Malawi 1 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Mozambique - Pinto Barros (85th), Tico Tico (87th)</p>
<p>Malawi - Jones Nkhwazi (62nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 35000</p>
<p>Final group standings (tabulate under played, won, drew, lsot, goals for, goal against):</p>
<p>    Zambia     6  4  2  0  9  3  14</p>
<p>    Mozambique 6  3  1  2  10 7  10</p>
<p>    Malawi     6  3  0  3  9  10 9</p>
<p>    Mauritius  6  0  1  5  4  11 1</p>
<p>Zambia and Mozambique qualify</p>
